meta {
  name: Switch device server (prod/dev)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/devices/:id/server
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  id: {{deviceId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "mode": "dev"
  }
}

docs {
  Points the boat at PROD (Render) or DEV (this backend's LAN address + port).

  - mode=prod: sys.server = https://indietrotutta.onrender.com
  - mode=dev with no host: sys.server = http://<this machine's LAN ip>:3000
  - mode=dev with host: sys.server = http://<host>

  Proxied to the device portal over LAN (POST http://<device-ip>/server?mode=...),
  so it needs a known device ip: 409 when the boat never heartbeated on a LAN,
  502 when the portal does not answer. Writes are POST-only; the device owns the
  choice in NVS, and the response is its own {mode, host, base} reply.
}
